Current Research
======
**The morphodynamic response of an active delta under sea-level fall** (PhD, Texas A&M University)

I am studying how falling sea level makes river channels in deltas cut down into the land (channel incision). I am also trying to quantify the different responses of the delta under the said forcings. I use numerical modeling with [pyDeltaRCM](https://deltarcm.org/pyDeltaRCM/index.html) and the [Sandpiper toolchain](https://sandpiper-toolchain.org/sandplover/), together with  analytical modelling based on mass balance concepts.

Past Research
======
**Mid-Channel Bar Dynamics of the Bhagirathi-Hooghly River** (M.Sc. thesis, Jadavpur University)

Mid-channel bars are sandy landforms that build up in the middle of a river where the flow slows down enough for sediment to settle. I studied how these bars changed from 1992 to 2023 along the Bhagirathi-Hooghly River in India, comparing the reach affected by tides with the reach that isn't, using Nabadwip as the dividing point.

[Read the book chapter](https://doi.org/10.1201/9781003545606-7)

**Plunge Pools and Pothole Growth, Kalikhola River** (M.Sc. project)

I studied how potholes and plunge pools grow in the bedrock of the Kalikhola River, and what controls their growth, by measuring their shape in the field at Rampuria.

